# Re-read After Compaction

## Why this earns alwaysApply
Forgetting repo conventions mid-session costs real time. It applies to almost every long edit. It stays tiny.

## Hard rules
1. **After any compaction, long pause, or "continue" handoff**, re-read before coding:
   - `AGENTS.md` (or `CLAUDE.md` if that is the source of truth)
   - Open TODO / PR description / decision notes in-repo
   - The `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` that match the files you will touch
2. **Do not invent a second stack.** If the repo uses TanStack Query, zod at the boundary, or Spring DTOs — keep that. Do not add a parallel data-fetching or validation style "while you are here."
3. **Persist durable decisions on disk**, not only in chat. If you chose an approach, write one line into `AGENTS.md` or `docs/decisions/` before the next compaction can erase it.
4. **If memory and the open files disagree**, stop and ask — do not silently override either.

## Quick recovery checklist
- [ ] Re-read AGENTS.md
- [ ] Confirm the stated Goal / Out of scope / Done when
- [ ] Confirm stack conventions for the files in scope
- [ ] Continue only the requested change

